 (R/'ethos_structural_evidence_contract_v1_design.json').write_text(json.dumps(design,indent=2,sort_keys=True)+'\n');(R/'ethos_task12u_contract_traceability.json').write_text(json.dumps(trace,indent=2,sort_keys=True)+'\n');(R/'ethos_task12u_contract_abuse_review.json').write_text(json.dumps(abuse,indent=2,sort_keys=True)+'\n')
 (R/'ETHOS_STRUCTURAL_EVIDENCE_CONTRACT_V1_DESIGN.md').write_text('# Structural Evidence Contract V1 — Design Only\n\n## Purpose\n\nRepresent what was declared, observed, derived, verified, and supplied structurally for N≥1 participants, without deciding ethical meaning.\n\n## Core design\n\nV1 uses scoped neutral entities, immutable assertion envelopes, a controlled/versioned neutral relation vocabulary, relation-based multi-actor event participation/targeting, task entities, separate verification, fact-specific authority policy outside data, lineage, conflicts, temporal availability, and first-class UNKNOWN. It is not an unbounded semantic graph.\n\n## Boundaries\n\nAssertor, actor, observer, target, requester, authorizer, verifier, role, authority, and responsibility are distinct where relevant. Assertions never become verified facts merely because they exist. Derived facts retain parents/rule/version and cannot gain authority. Conflict is retained, repetition does not prove independence, and post-action facts cannot leak into pre-action decisions.\n\n## Neutrality\n\nNeutral facts include identities, event/task/target bindings, ordering, completion, deadlines, outcomes, authorization, provenance, and assignment. Ethical abandonment, responsibility displacement, unethical delegation, RAF/TCF conclusions, scores, and violations are prohibited.\n\n## Compatibility and readiness\n\nV1 is additive: Greed, Pride, Envy, V2.1, EvidenceView, factual context, admission, and the gate are unchanged and need not consume it. Generic action facts could also be useful to a future Wrath research consumer without encoding Wrath.\n\n**STRUCTURAL EVIDENCE CONTRACT V1 READY FOR ADVERSARIAL DESIGN REVIEW.** This does not authorize implementation.\n')
